Expose Copilot's per-model reasoning effort in the model picker

Port of alfdupont/happier commit 1b8e2a307e ("fix(cli): expose Copilot's
per-model reasoning effort in the model picker") to the bundled
package-dist of the happier-cli 0.2.14 release. Apply from the root of the
extracted release tree with `patch -p1`.

The preflight model probe returned ACP-listed models as soon as the agent
reported a `models` list. That dropped the model-scoped config options (such
as `reasoning_effort`), so the new-session picker showed no effort control
for any Copilot model. ACP reports those options only for the session's
current model, and Copilot's effort levels differ per model, so for agents
that declare `acpModelOptionsScope: "per_model"` the probe selects each
listed model on its disposable probe session and records that model's
options, within the probe's existing deadline.

- withMcpTimeout-*.mjs (bundled @happier-dev/agents): Copilot declares
  `acpModelOptionsScope: "per_model"`.
- api-*.mjs (bundled agentModelsProbe): attach the session's model-scoped
  options to models from either source, and walk per-model agents' models.

The probe source in 0.2.14 is identical to the commit's parent, so this is a
line-for-line translation of the commit into the bundled JavaScript.

